{"archetypes":[{"name":"oos-pipeline","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes the end-to-end accepted-OOS artifact flow across tally, emit, review-and-fix, and disposition gates.","prompt_body":"Trace the accepted-OOS lifecycle across tally-code-votes.sh, emit-tally.sh, review-and-fix.sh, accumulated artifacts, and disposition gates. Check whether preserve, serialize, rebuild, mirror, or truncate paths can still drop, duplicate, renumber, or publicize blocks incorrectly across review-core, standalone, nested implement, and coder-SKIPPED flows. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The implementation relies on Bash, awk, regex, temp files, and macOS/Bash 3.2 portability-sensitive constructs.","prompt_body":"Inspect the new and changed shell and awk code for Bash 3.2, BSD awk/sed, quoting, temp-file, pipeline, and process-substitution portability hazards. Pay special attention to normalization helpers, block splitting, counters, command substitutions, and error handling under empty or malformed inputs. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"reader-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff updates both Python and awk readers that must classify OOS markdown identically.","prompt_body":"Compare the Python OOS parser and the awk non-security block counter for semantic parity on canonical OOS headers, legacy tagged FINDING headers, bare FINDING headers, security exclusions, and multi-block markdown. Look for regex or state-machine differences that could make bash gates and Python gates disagree. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-contracts","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The patch introduces a shared normalization contract and updates multiple docs/tests that must remain consistent with runtime behavior.","prompt_body":"Review whether the new normalize-oos-block-header contract, caller documentation, Makefile harness registration, and regression tests match the actual runtime behavior. Check for mismatches between documented acceptance criteria and implemented branches, especially around fallback serialization, sequence initialization, and security-tag handling. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
